  "limitations": "Autonomous affine linear systems only, dimension 1..8 and at most 10000 fixed steps. Not RK45, not a complete adaptive integrator, no stiffness handling, events, dense output, spacecraft model or global-error certificate. Keep physical units consistent between matrix, bias, times and state. Overflow is rejected. The raw upstream terr omits h; treating it as a state error would be dimensionally wrong.",
  "port_notes": "Preserves all 13 stages and the exact upstream xf weights; returns last_error_indicator=(41/840)*(f0+f10-f11-f12) exactly as the Fortran routine does, WITHOUT h. last_local_error_estimate=h*last_error_indicator is an explicitly derived adapter field, not an upstream output and not a global error bound. Adds a fixed-step loop and limits the callback to matrix*y+bias. The source cites Fehlberg NASA 1968; this is a modern Fortran implementation of that classic formula, not a claim that the repository contains 1968 source. No Fortran compiler was available, so the original Fortran binary was not executed.",
